# Web + mobile parity

When changing product UI or user-facing behavior, **update both platforms in the same task** unless the user explicitly says web-only or mobile-only.

## Platforms

| Surface | Typical paths |
|---|---|
| Web (Next.js) | `app/`, `components/`, `lib/` |
| Mobile (Expo) | `mobile/src/screens/`, `mobile/src/components/`, `mobile/src/lib/` |

Mirror shared logic under both `lib/` and `mobile/src/lib/` when the feature exists on both (invite flows, clinical tests, consulta adaptive, clinic hub, reports, etc.).

## Screen size

- Do **not** copy desktop layouts onto mobile.
- Mobile: touch targets, safe areas, ScrollView nesting rules, compact headers, no hover-only actions.
- Web: keep existing desktop/tablet patterns; still check narrow viewports when the change is layout-heavy.
- Same **behavior and labels**; different **layout/spacing** as needed for each screen.

## Checklist before finishing

1. Web change done
2. Matching mobile change done (or confirmed N/A)
3. Shared constants/helpers synced if duplicated
4. i18n keys updated on mobile when copy changes
